      <h2 id="the-labs">The Labs</h2>
      <p>Modern forensic genealogy labs &mdash; Othram among them &mdash; are specialist vendors that bridge conventional forensics and genealogy. At a high level, they receive evidence or extracts, assess how degraded or limited the sample is, choose a method to generate the detailed genetic profile, upload to permitted databases, analyze the matches, and hand investigators a report explaining likely family relationships and recommended next steps.</p>
      <p>They&rsquo;re often in the news because they specialize in the hardest samples &mdash; old, trace, or degraded material that defeats standard testing. But no lab solves a case alone. Even after a promising genealogy result, investigators and public crime labs still have to do the direct confirmation testing, the records work, and the legal case-building. The science opens a door; people still have to walk through it.</p>
      <p class="post__note">For a step-by-step look at how one of these labs fits into a case, see <a href="/how-othram-works-in-a-case/">How Othram Works in a Case</a>.</p>

